ain in  the movie  Harvey Dent was played by Aaron Eckhart  he was the district attorney for Gotham  City and he wasn't always very ethical  in fact the cops called him Harvey  two-face I heard they have a different  name for me down at MCU that name soon  turns literal when his face is de  figured by fire Danton refuses any skin  grafts and he becomes the villain  two-face it's a really creepy look and  the scene where he reveals his new face  is terrifying but what does that seem  look like without CGI well he looks like  Aaron Eckhart she's got some emotion  captured on his face and it's not scary  at all it's amazing how much the CGI  changed him they definitely could not  have achieved the same level of gore  we'd just make up in 2012 director  Angley brought a best-selling novel to  life on the big screen Life of Pi was a  huge success critics loved it and it  made over six hundred million dollars  worldwide it won four Oscars and one of  those awards was for Best Visual Effects  Life of Pi was about a family from India  who owned a zoo they closed their zoo  and decide to move to Canada to sell the  animals oh shoot  gravy is not meat is taste but there is  a shipwreck and pie is the only human  survivor she has to survive months on  his own and his only companion is a  ferocious tiger they share a small boat  and learn to help and appreciate each  other it's an amazing movie and the  scenes with the tiger are so cool but  when you see the clips of the movie  without the digital effects its  underwhelming in fact it's absolutely  hilarious at times Suraj Sharma plays  spy and he looks at way less cool on an  empty boat in the swimming pool you'll  probably notice there's no Tiger which  is probably a lot safer one of the  sweetest scenes in the movie is when the  tiger lays his head on PI's lap but that  didn't really happen  check out the tiger stunt double it's a  badly  blue stuffed animal with permanent  marker eyes superhero movies always rely  on a lot 