ual effects and deep  political messages the movie is about  humans who are colonizing a planet that  is home to a peaceful alien race the  military sends soldiers in as avatars of  the Navi race to study the world one of  these soldiers is attacked and rescued  by Zoe Saldana's character net teary but  Zoe Saldana isn't a blue alien the movie  relied heavily on motion capture  animation to turn the actors into Navi  aliens when you see clips of Avatar  without the CGI it's not nearly as  exciting  Zoe looks way less fierce we loved that  they added fake ears to her mocap suit  thanks to some impressive CGI audiences  were able to lose themselves in the  beautiful world of Pandora as always  held out may be great at motion capture  but there is one actor who is the king  of mocap acting keep watching to find  out who it is oh no  the Harry Potter franchise spared no  expense in bringing the Wizarding World  to life all of the movies use  cutting-edge digital effects things like  Quidditch and the various fantastic  beasts are all done with the help of CGI  but every now and then the directors  went old-school Daniel Radcliffe has  revealed that one of the scariest scenes  was really not terrifying at all in  Deathly Hallows Part 1 Harry and  Hermione go to Godric's Hollow to find  Bathilda Bagshot what they don't know is  that Bathilda isn't really pathetic  she's actually Voldemort snake Nagini in  disguise she lures Harry upstairs in the  form of the old lady then she transforms  and attacks fans jumped and shrieked in  the theatres but there is no scary snake  on set for the attack scene makini was  just a long pole that had a boxing glove  tied to the end someone thrust the pole  at Daniel Radcliffe later the effects  team replaced the pole with a giant  snake it all seems way less terrifying  sometimes you don't need a high-tech  solution let me give you a cut again the  first Pirates of the Caribbean movie was  such a success that Disney created four  sequels 